WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.488
Assessors want five things
from configuration management,

2
00:00:03.488 --> 00:00:06.238
and Ansible can show each
one without extra work.

3
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:10.587
The baseline is simply the playbook
version, by Git commit and tag.

4
00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:14.263
Change control is the pull
request with a required reviewer.

5
00:00:14.263 --> 00:00:18.684
The same playbook that applies settings
can run in check mode to report drift,

6
00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:21.862
so implementation and monitoring
come from one source.

7
00:00:21.862 --> 00:00:25.438
Removing packages you don't
need shows least functionality.

8
00:00:25.438 --> 00:00:30.362
And because the inventory comes from the
C M D B, Ansible never invents a host,

9
00:00:30.362 --> 00:00:34.651
and anything it couldn't reach says
so instead of passing quietly.

10
00:00:34.651 --> 00:00:36.740
Here's where all that evidence goes.
